<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Prices steady, trade slow.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Prices steady, trade slow.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat prices remained mostly steady on Wednesday as several dealers noted a pickup in movement early in the session.</p>
<p>&quot;We have taken in quite a bit,&quot; one Montana dealer said, referring to winter wheat sales by farmers.</p>
<p>But the dealer said spring wheat acreage was expected to be down and that producers were holding on to their spring wheat for a little while longer.</p>
<p>Another Montana merchandiser said his firm bought a few cars this morning but activity died down later in the day.</p>
<p>MGE May futures gained 1/4 cent to end at $4.00-3/4 a bushel.</p>
